# ================================
# BLANKET SLICE, LAMINAR STAGE L2: L1 + NUCLEAR (VOLUMETRIC) HEATING IN THE EUROFER
#   NUCLEAR  : Q = 1.6e6 exp(-d / 0.15 m) W/m3, d = DEPTH FROM THE FIRST WALL y = 0.28 m
#              (ONE FIFTH OF THE ~8 MW/m3 DEMO FIRST-WALL PEAK, SAME SCALE AS THE FLUX)
#   COOLANT  : WATER, CONSTANT PROPERTIES AT 298 K (blanket.matprop, ID 0)
#   SOLID    : EUROFER97 (ID 1)
#   INLETS   : BC 511, TOTAL 0.050 kg/s OVER THE 4 INLETS, 298.15 K
#              (Re ~ 1870 / 1250 / 1250 / 620 IN CHANNELS 1-4)
#   OUTLETS  : BC 520, 0 Pa GAUGE
#   HEATING  : BC 532 (FRONT FACE + R6 FILLETS) 1.0e5 W/m2
#   OUTPUT   : ONE .pvtu EVERY 50000 ITERATIONS (~0.3 GB EACH AT h5) AND AT THE STOP
#   STEADY   : STOPS WHEN RelU,V,W < l2norm_vel AND RelT < l2norm_temp
#              (AFTER steady_min_iterations); CHECK THE ENERGY BALANCE AFTER.
# LINES STARTING WITH # ARE COMMENTS.
# ================================
